blocks.en:
We evaluate action-conditioned video prediction on five cross-embodiment benchmarks spanning distinct embodiments and data sources:
(i) the DreamDojo benchmarks [ 34 ] , three Fourier GR-1 robot evaluation sets from DreamDojo: In-lab (100 clips), EgoDex (65 clips), and DreamDojo-HV (68 clips);
(ii) Ψ 0 \Psi_{0} [ 117 ] , 100 evaluation windows of dexterous humanoid manipulation recorded with the Ψ 0 \Psi_{0} vision-language-action (VLA) system (50 seen-task, 50 unseen-task);
(iii) ω \omega -HOME [ 65 ] , 100 evaluation windows of household loco-manipulation on a Unitree G1 humanoid with dexterous five-finger hands across 24 tasks (50 seen, 50 from five held-out tasks);
(iv) Xp-Teleop (Sec. 5 ), 100 evaluation windows of long-horizon dexterous humanoid teleoperation, split by scene (50 windows from held-out takes of training scenes, 50 from unseen scenes);
and (v) AgiBot [ 15 ] , 50 held-out windows of gripper-based manipulation, where all compared models include AgiBot data in training.
In addition, we report zero-shot prediction on 200 held-out human egocentric clips (EgoSuite and OpenAoE; Sec. 6.2 ).

